Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/spocc-spabund-users/c/h9NzHMmm6RY/m/ISsIBSsAAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear Group,

I have been using spOccupancy for some time now to and find it to be an excellent package, thank you developing this resource. Specifically I have used the function stPGOcc to fit spatiotemporal occupancy models with good success. However, a couple of my focal species are quite common and I am interested in fitting models in spAbundance for those species. I have gotten the NMix function to work with a site-level random intercept to three years of data but ideally the model would also to include a spatial component.

Is it possible to fit a model using spNMix when you have multiple observations from the same site (i.e., a stacked model)?

Any information on this topic would be greatly appreciated

Sean

